        "data": {
          "id": "PromptTemplate-flaky",
          "node": {
            "display_name": "Prompt Template",
            "description": "Compare two Playwright JSON reports and classify flaky tests.",
            "icon": "Braces",
            "name": "PromptTemplate",
            "lf_version": "1.12.1",
            "template": {
              "_type": "Component",
              "report1": {
                "_input_type": "MessageTextInput",
                "display_name": "Report 1",
                "name": "report1",
                "type": "str",
                "required": true,
                "value": ""
              },
              "report2": {
                "_input_type": "MessageTextInput",
                "display_name": "Report 2",
                "name": "report2",
                "type": "str",
                "required": true,
                "value": ""
              },
              "user_instruction": {
                "_input_type": "MessageTextInput",
                "display_name": "User Instruction",
                "name": "user_instruction",
                "type": "str",
                "required": false,
                "value": ""
              },
              "template": {
                "_input_type": "PromptInput",
                "display_name": "Template",
                "name": "template",
                "type": "str",
                "required": true,
                "value": "You are a QA architect analyzing Playwright test reports.\n\nPLAYWRIGHT_REPORT1_FOLDER (repeated runs):\n{report1}\n\nPLAYWRIGHT_REPORT2_FOLDER (repeated runs):\n{report2}\n\nUSER INSTRUCTION:\n{user_instruction}\n\nEach input contains the JSON results from every file in one folder. Treat result1/result2 as repeated runs of one suite and result3/result4 as repeated runs of another suite. Parse every JSON array and match tests by exact title within each folder. A test is flaky only when the same title has different statuses across repeated runs, such as passed in one run and failed in another. A test that fails in every run is consistently failing, not flaky. A test that passes in every run is stable. Analyze both folders and combine their findings. Do not compare unrelated title namespaces across folders.\n\nReturn valid JSON only, using this schema:\n{\"flaky_test_count\": 0, \"flaky_tests\": [{\"title\": \"...\", \"folder\": \"...\", \"statuses\": [\"passed\", \"failed\"], \"reason\": \"...\"}], \"stable_test_count\": 0, \"consistently_failing_test_count\": 0, \"unmatched_test_count\": 0, \"unmatched_tests\": [], \"summary\": \"...\"}"
              }
            },
            "outputs": [
